WEBVTT

00:57.140 --> 00:59.392
There's this phrase in The Art of War.

00:59.976 --> 01:02.187
"The best defense is a good offense."

01:02.771 --> 01:05.398
Um, but you know, I don't exactly agree.

01:05.482 --> 01:07.817
It's already hard to defend yourself.

01:07.901 --> 01:09.152
You won't have any strength.

01:09.235 --> 01:11.988
So in my own opinion, the best defense

01:12.906 --> 01:14.157
is running away.

01:14.783 --> 01:15.909
UNG IN ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

01:15.992 --> 01:18.995
I have a very long history
of running away.

01:19.079 --> 01:23.917
All right, the student to present
about his beloved family in third period

01:24.000 --> 01:25.043
is Choi Ung.

01:25.126 --> 01:26.753
Ung, are you ready?

01:27.837 --> 01:31.758
We will just take a short break first,
and then we will begin, okay?

01:31.841 --> 01:33.301
Okay!

01:44.020 --> 01:46.940
Ung, come down. Come on!

01:47.023 --> 01:48.233
Come down!

01:48.316 --> 01:50.026
Ung, come down from that tree!

01:50.110 --> 01:51.569
At quite a young age…

01:51.653 --> 01:54.614
Ung, come down from there, please.

01:54.697 --> 01:56.991
You could get hurt. You can't stay there.

01:57.075 --> 01:59.661
I won't let you do the presentation,
so come down.

01:59.744 --> 02:00.829
I mean it, I won't.

02:00.912 --> 02:03.414
See? Pinky promise.
I won't make you do it.

02:03.498 --> 02:06.543
- …I tasted the sweetness of it all.
- Come down, all right?

02:07.877 --> 02:11.589
UNG IN HIGH SCHOOL

02:11.673 --> 02:14.884
Of course, I run away for my sake.

02:14.968 --> 02:16.010
Choi Ung!

02:16.594 --> 02:19.097
That brat completely broke this thing.

02:19.180 --> 02:22.517
- You brat! Stop right there!
- But also for the other person.

02:22.600 --> 02:24.060
Look at what you did, jerk!

02:24.144 --> 02:25.895
I am buying time for them

02:25.979 --> 02:28.898
so that we can have
a calm conversation later.

02:30.608 --> 02:32.986
This cost 29,900 won!

02:34.696 --> 02:36.114
UNG IN UNIVERSITY

02:36.197 --> 02:38.158
Wait, I won't hit you!

02:41.828 --> 02:43.037
And I won't yell at you.

02:43.621 --> 02:44.789
So come here.

02:45.748 --> 02:47.709
So that we can have
a calm conversation,

02:48.459 --> 02:49.794
I am buying time for them.

02:49.878 --> 02:50.920
Do you mean it?

02:53.965 --> 02:55.091
Come here.

02:58.136 --> 03:00.138
Stop right there!

03:02.056 --> 03:05.435
That doesn't mean
I always run from everything.

03:06.102 --> 03:09.230
- Is it because you're entering a marathon?
- Mm-hmm.

03:09.314 --> 03:11.357
Yeon-su said that
if I do the half marathon,

03:11.441 --> 03:12.859
we'll wear matching rings.

03:14.903 --> 03:16.738
She really is amazing, huh?

03:18.072 --> 03:20.825
Is she dating or babysitting you?

03:20.909 --> 03:22.744
She still doesn't know me well.

03:22.827 --> 03:24.245
I'm a man of my word.

03:25.038 --> 03:28.374
Hey, listen. I'm gonna give you
some tough training,

03:28.458 --> 03:30.335
so don't you dare go back on your word.

03:30.418 --> 03:32.253
We're running for an hour every day.

03:32.337 --> 03:33.463
Yeah, yeah. I know.

03:33.546 --> 03:35.423
A half marathon is a cake walk.

03:35.506 --> 03:37.300
I could probably
complete the full marathon.

03:37.967 --> 03:39.052
Eat my dust.

03:41.679 --> 03:42.764
Jeez.

03:47.393 --> 03:49.229
- Get going.
- No.

03:51.898 --> 03:53.983
No, I can't do this anymore.

03:55.151 --> 03:56.945
- Come on.
- No!

04:24.472 --> 04:25.807
INCOMING CALL
KIM JI-UNG

04:28.101 --> 04:31.854
I make objective judgments
to make the best decision.

04:31.938 --> 04:33.398
INCOMING CALL
KIM JI-UNG

04:37.944 --> 04:41.864
Right. I can just wear
matching rings with Ji-ung.

04:41.948 --> 04:43.074
Right. Right.

04:53.376 --> 04:56.379
So I'm not embarrassed about running away.

04:56.462 --> 04:59.716
UNG IN THE PRESENT

05:07.056 --> 05:08.474
It's been way too long,

05:10.643 --> 05:12.228
we should be able to…

05:13.104 --> 05:14.689
ask each other "How have you been?"

05:16.107 --> 05:17.358
"How tough has it been for you?"

05:19.777 --> 05:22.280
"It's been tough for me."
We're allowed to say those things.

05:23.656 --> 05:25.074
Damn it…

05:32.915 --> 05:35.460
I asked you
for a writer a long time ago, didn't I?

05:35.543 --> 05:37.086
Are you sending me one, huh?

05:37.170 --> 05:39.714
Well, about that, you know…

05:42.550 --> 05:45.470
I did my best to find one for you,
so don't blame me for this, okay?

05:45.553 --> 05:47.472
Everyone is working on something.

05:47.555 --> 05:49.891
Which means,
no one is available to send to you.

05:49.974 --> 05:51.059
So sadly…

05:51.559 --> 05:54.187
Hmm, anyway, good luck, all right.

05:54.771 --> 05:57.231
What's this? Who is it?
Why are you making such excuses?

06:06.366 --> 06:08.743
Come on in already.

06:08.826 --> 06:10.745
Are you just going to stand there all day?

06:11.871 --> 06:14.248
You know you're overqualified
to be working on this.

06:14.332 --> 06:16.334
So what are you doing in here, huh?

06:16.417 --> 06:18.336
It's just a simple project.

06:18.419 --> 06:20.671
You know what, I'll just get
one of the rookie writers to help.

06:20.755 --> 06:23.007
Why? Do you think I wanted to do this?

06:23.091 --> 06:26.719
Mr. Park was desperately
asking for my help.

06:26.803 --> 06:28.888
You said you were gonna work
on dramas now.

06:28.971 --> 06:31.432
- So just go and write one instead of--
- Well, I am.

06:31.516 --> 06:34.560
I hate it when people tell me to write
when I already am.

06:35.103 --> 06:36.854
I came here to clear my head a bit,

06:36.938 --> 06:39.482
so please, don't be so obvious
about hating me being here.

06:40.400 --> 06:43.778
- Are trying to have your way?
- That's what makes them great.

06:43.861 --> 06:45.446
I don't want you on this.

06:45.530 --> 06:48.950
- I…
- I saw the preview, and it was awful.

06:50.326 --> 06:51.994
Who said you could show her?

06:52.078 --> 06:55.456
Mr. Kim… what in the world
are you trying to film here?

06:55.540 --> 06:58.918
I don't get what you're trying to say
through these videos that you shot.

06:59.001 --> 07:01.254
What the hell has gotten into you?

07:01.337 --> 07:03.464
- Have you lost your touch?
- Okay, you know something,

07:03.548 --> 07:07.051
I'll take care of this myself,
so go the hell back to where you came from

07:07.135 --> 07:10.471
or go clear your head somewhere else
as long as it's away from me an my crew!

07:10.555 --> 07:11.514
Mr. Kim.

07:13.850 --> 07:16.894
We're in a bad situation.
We really do need a writer.

07:17.937 --> 07:21.107
Well, I do have something to make up for.

07:22.400 --> 07:24.527
I won't be that stubborn this time.

07:36.038 --> 07:37.206
All right then…

07:39.208 --> 07:40.543
what is it you have in mind?

07:43.129 --> 07:46.466
I heard that the cast are your friends.
Is that why you were lazy?

07:48.050 --> 07:51.888
Well, honestly,
I was thinking of refusing this project.

07:53.097 --> 07:56.517
But as I kept watching,
I found something interesting.

07:56.601 --> 07:58.978
So I watched the documentary
from ten years ago.

07:59.061 --> 08:01.481
- So what?
- There seemed to be something

08:01.564 --> 08:04.108
going on between the two of them, no?

08:07.445 --> 08:10.406
There is no way
that you wouldn't have noticed that.

08:11.991 --> 08:15.453
If we write a story based on that,
it'd be quite a show.

08:15.536 --> 08:17.955
I don't want to make anything up.

08:18.581 --> 08:20.583
No, it actually felt like,

08:20.666 --> 08:25.379
like the camera was purposely trying
to ignore that part, you know what I mean?

08:26.589 --> 08:29.425
- But then, that was just me.
- Why would I do that intentionally?

08:29.509 --> 08:31.511
I was just trying
to film objectively and--

08:31.594 --> 08:33.721
Then why the heck
would people film things?

08:33.804 --> 08:36.224
You can just let machines
do all the shooting then.

08:36.307 --> 08:40.269
My goodness. You really haven't
changed a bit, Mr. Kim.

08:42.271 --> 08:46.692
Well, at the very least,
you made the scenes look quite pretty.

08:47.443 --> 08:48.903
I'll just whip something up…

08:50.029 --> 08:51.614
based on them.

08:59.997 --> 09:01.249
- Oh, hey, you're up.
- Hey.

09:01.332 --> 09:02.833
We're having a party today, all right?

09:02.917 --> 09:04.293
Look behind you.

09:05.753 --> 09:09.006
I put in so much effort
to prepare your debut anniversary party.

09:10.299 --> 09:12.468
Oh, right. Yeon-su's coming too
because we're filming.

09:14.762 --> 09:16.764
Now is there anyone else
I forgot to invite?

09:17.348 --> 09:18.933
Maybe someone like NJ would like to come.

09:19.016 --> 09:20.142
Like NJ, you know.

09:20.226 --> 09:21.435
Or just NJ.

09:24.230 --> 09:26.315
Right, Ji-ung said
he's coming early today.

09:26.399 --> 09:27.858
I should prepare this.

09:30.194 --> 09:33.531
Ung! Ji-ung said he's coming over first
so go and get ready, okay?

09:33.614 --> 09:37.076
By running away,
I'm not avoiding anything,

09:37.159 --> 09:38.869
 it's a reasonable decision.

09:40.705 --> 09:41.872
Okay.

09:52.466 --> 09:53.593
Running away?

09:56.929 --> 10:01.601
Running away from things is something
only cowardly people would do.

10:13.029 --> 10:16.991
I've never run away from anything,
not once in my life.

10:24.206 --> 10:25.416
Sorry.

10:26.959 --> 10:28.878
Uh, I'm quite drunk right now, Ung.

10:38.929 --> 10:43.601
Has all nothing more than
a pathetic excuse that they used.

10:47.146 --> 10:48.314
Let's get some coffee.

10:51.400 --> 10:52.568
So then?

10:52.652 --> 10:54.528
Have you read all my draft?

10:57.239 --> 10:58.616
I guess you haven't yet.

10:58.699 --> 11:02.787
I'm sure you wouldn't be making faces
after reading such an amazing draft.

11:02.870 --> 11:05.247
Sorry, but we can't film

11:05.331 --> 11:08.125
- this amazing story of yours.
- What? Why?

11:10.378 --> 11:15.424
Mr. Kim. Don't you think it's a bit
too childish to reject my works like this?

11:16.133 --> 11:17.843
- They ran away.
- Who did?

11:17.927 --> 11:20.012
- The cast.
- Who exactly in the cast?

11:20.096 --> 11:22.056
Choi Ung.

11:22.723 --> 11:24.600
Go get him then. It's no big deal.

11:24.684 --> 11:26.102
And Kook Yeon-su.

11:31.941 --> 11:34.652
EPISODE 7
CATCH ME IF YOU CAN

11:34.735 --> 11:40.408
CELEBRATION PARTY
CHOI UNG, KOOK YEON-SU

11:41.158 --> 11:44.245
ONE HOUR EARLIER

11:53.713 --> 11:56.465
I told you I called him several times.
It's useless.

11:56.549 --> 11:58.342
You said you were
with him this morning, right?

11:58.426 --> 12:02.012
Hm. He was here earlier,
but he just disappeared.

12:02.096 --> 12:04.473
Did you really not hear
anything from Yeon-su?

12:04.557 --> 12:05.808
Oh, you mean me?

12:06.726 --> 12:09.729
You see all these wine bottles?
These are the ones I brought.

12:09.812 --> 12:11.939
I went to the trouble
of closing my bar today,

12:12.022 --> 12:14.984
so I could attend this party.
And now what?

12:15.860 --> 12:17.445
Don't you think I'm a victim too?

12:17.528 --> 12:20.281
I get Choi Ung
would do something like this,

12:20.364 --> 12:22.199
but Yeon-su is not that irresponsible.

12:23.576 --> 12:25.911
You don't think maybe something
happened to them, do you?

12:25.995 --> 12:27.955
Didn't you take her home last night?

12:28.539 --> 12:30.499
Does she still have a hangover?

12:30.583 --> 12:33.043
I remember she barely does.

12:33.127 --> 12:34.545
I'll try calling her grandma.

12:38.632 --> 12:39.925
Hmm.

12:40.593 --> 12:43.846
- What? Is it Yeon-su?
- She did go AWOL.

12:44.805 --> 12:49.185
"I need some time to think.
Don't tell my grandma anything."

12:49.977 --> 12:52.813
Judging from that rude text,
it looks like she hasn't been kidnapped.

12:52.897 --> 12:54.482
Yeon-su went AWOL?

12:54.565 --> 12:57.193
- Why? What for?
- Now where could Ung be?

12:57.276 --> 12:59.653
Oh, you know the guy. He can be so simple.

12:59.737 --> 13:02.782
If we just look around the neighborhood,
we'll find him right away. Don't worry.

13:03.407 --> 13:05.951
Why is he suddenly doing this?

13:06.035 --> 13:08.287
The drawing show went well yesterday.

13:08.370 --> 13:10.748
I really don't get it.

13:10.831 --> 13:14.752
Isn't it a bit strange for them
to do this at the same time?

13:14.835 --> 13:17.880
I mean, maybe something happened
between the two of them.

13:19.256 --> 13:20.216
Don't you think?

13:21.383 --> 13:22.551
Or is it just me?

13:22.635 --> 13:25.304
No way. I didn't actually see them
together yesterday, though.

13:25.888 --> 13:29.558
Right. And Yeon-su came into my bar
right after it ended,

13:29.642 --> 13:32.102
and then she got drunk,
and then she went straight home.

13:32.186 --> 13:34.605
Ung was tired
and went to bed early last night too.

13:55.209 --> 13:57.711
Was I really drunk last night?

13:59.338 --> 14:00.506
No way.

14:00.589 --> 14:03.342
Did I take pills yesterday?

14:06.262 --> 14:07.555
Nope.

14:07.638 --> 14:11.350
Did I still cry
in front of Yeon-su regardless?

14:27.074 --> 14:28.075
But…

14:28.993 --> 14:31.996
she probably won't remember anything
since she was drunk.

14:38.085 --> 14:39.670
GU EUN-HO

14:39.753 --> 14:42.965
You'll get caught anyway.
So just tell us where you are already.

14:43.048 --> 14:45.843
Is this because I asked you for a raise?
I'm not giving up, though.

14:45.926 --> 14:48.846
Are you with Yeon-su right now?
Why are you both suddenly going AWOL?

14:54.184 --> 14:57.187
I'll avoid it for now
and think things through later.

15:07.781 --> 15:09.950
Well, I did expect this, but…

15:10.743 --> 15:12.494
There's nowhere for me to go now.

15:14.121 --> 15:17.708
What do people usually do
when they're in my situation?

15:27.927 --> 15:28.886
Oh.

15:31.555 --> 15:33.474
I don't really have friends.

15:40.022 --> 15:42.232
I'm not running away.

15:42.316 --> 15:45.861
I'm just keeping my distance
until I can get my thoughts in order.

15:49.990 --> 15:51.909
This is so fun.

15:52.868 --> 15:53.953
Huh?

15:54.578 --> 15:56.455
The two of them ran away,
isn't that right?

15:59.750 --> 16:01.835
How exciting.
This is even better than I thought!

16:01.919 --> 16:04.380
Isn't it strange that they both went AWOL?

16:04.463 --> 16:06.090
A bit strange, yes.

16:06.173 --> 16:07.091
That's right.

16:07.967 --> 16:11.345
This is going to hit the jackpot.
Clearly, there must be something going on!

16:11.428 --> 16:14.264
I have to be able to film something
for it to hit the jackpot.

16:14.348 --> 16:16.642
And how can I do that
without any of the cast?

16:17.226 --> 16:19.019
What on earth has gotten into you?

16:19.103 --> 16:21.814
- You don't seem enthusiastic about this.
- What do you mean?

16:21.897 --> 16:24.775
When have you ever given up
just because the cast ran away?

16:24.858 --> 16:26.318
Remember what happened with Jukdo?

16:26.402 --> 16:27.695
Why would you bring that up?

16:27.778 --> 16:29.613
When you heard
that the whole cast went AWOL,

16:29.697 --> 16:31.824
you searched
the entire island for them, did you not?

16:31.907 --> 16:33.325
Plus, that snake farm.

16:33.409 --> 16:36.245
You ran around the mountain
looking for that snake that escaped.

16:36.328 --> 16:38.956
And now you're telling me that
you can't film just because of that?

16:39.039 --> 16:40.124
Even if I do find them,

16:40.207 --> 16:43.794
would I be able to film anything good
if I forced them to stay on camera?

16:43.877 --> 16:45.129
If you bring them back,

16:46.213 --> 16:48.340
make sure that
they can never run away again.

16:49.299 --> 16:51.427
Let's see…

16:52.928 --> 16:55.639
Would you prefer mountains or islands?

16:55.723 --> 16:56.890
Uh, what?

16:58.726 --> 17:00.269
Hey, you, Intern.

17:00.352 --> 17:03.022
What are my works most known for?

17:03.105 --> 17:05.190
Bringing out the primal emotions of people

17:05.274 --> 17:08.068
using limited space
in an unfamiliar environment.

17:08.152 --> 17:09.695
Say that simply.

17:10.571 --> 17:13.073
Locking up the cast?

17:13.157 --> 17:15.492
The weather's nice. So let's go on a trip.

17:16.535 --> 17:18.871
Kidnap the cast,
and take them somewhere secluded,

17:18.954 --> 17:20.789
and then film them for about three days.

17:21.623 --> 17:22.708
Okay?

17:24.960 --> 17:26.712
All right, all right,
don't worry.

17:26.795 --> 17:28.881
I'm doing my best to find him.

17:28.964 --> 17:31.550
Hmm. I'll call you once I find him.

17:31.633 --> 17:35.345
Oh, wait, there's a taxi. Taxi!
I'll just call you later, okay?

17:41.852 --> 17:43.062
Thank you, Choi Ung.

17:44.313 --> 17:46.482
Dobby is free. Thank you so much.

17:52.154 --> 17:53.322
Oh, my gosh! What the?

17:54.031 --> 17:57.076
- I was here the whole time by the way.
- What are you doing here?

17:57.826 --> 17:58.660
I got hungry.

17:58.744 --> 18:02.331
You know, there's a lot of food here,
but there's nothing to eat.

18:02.414 --> 18:04.041
Wait, you didn't leave?

18:04.750 --> 18:06.919
- Nobody told me to.
- But everyone already left.

18:07.002 --> 18:08.337
My bottles are still here.

18:08.420 --> 18:10.464
I mean, shouldn't you
be looking for Yeon-su?

18:10.547 --> 18:11.548
What about you?

18:12.424 --> 18:15.511
Hold it, why are you
talking so casually to me right now?

18:15.594 --> 18:19.598
Oh, well, I strongly support and believe
in a hierarchy based on someone's age.

18:19.681 --> 18:21.725
And I happen to be older than you.

18:21.809 --> 18:23.977
So, you really don't know
where Ung is, huh?

18:24.061 --> 18:25.729
Oh, of course I do.

18:25.813 --> 18:28.357
It's obvious where he most likely went.

18:28.440 --> 18:30.442
He doesn't have any friends or hobbies.

18:30.526 --> 18:31.985
It's the same for Yeon-su.

18:32.069 --> 18:34.154
You think that's the reason
why they dated?

18:35.155 --> 18:37.366
I guess he does have
something like a hobby.

18:37.449 --> 18:39.076
It's obvious.

18:39.159 --> 18:41.286
Those two are together right now.

18:42.454 --> 18:44.915
Isn't this your first time
coming to this house, though?

18:45.499 --> 18:47.709
How come you're acting
like you own the place, huh?

18:47.793 --> 18:49.878
Well, I came here to have fun,

18:49.962 --> 18:51.755
and I did close my bar for this.

18:52.339 --> 18:53.924
I can't just sit around.

18:56.510 --> 18:58.971
How about a party without them?

19:04.393 --> 19:05.310
Sol-i.

19:06.103 --> 19:07.312
You're such a genius.

19:22.619 --> 19:24.913
It feels like I've already come back

19:24.997 --> 19:27.624
only three hours after I ran away.

19:28.500 --> 19:31.461
I ended up
right in front of Ung again.

19:32.921 --> 19:34.089
Hi.

19:34.173 --> 19:35.132
Okay, that's it.

19:35.215 --> 19:37.843
That's the worst thing
I said this entire year.

19:38.677 --> 19:39.928
Mm.

19:42.347 --> 19:43.515
Hey, so…

19:44.266 --> 19:45.475
What are you doing here?

19:48.312 --> 19:49.396
Oh.

19:50.522 --> 19:51.773
I thought you…

19:53.984 --> 19:56.069
were doing a celebration party today.

19:56.153 --> 19:57.404
What about you?

19:57.487 --> 19:59.448
Uh…

19:59.531 --> 20:01.033
I wanted to get some rest.

20:02.701 --> 20:04.703
Mm.

20:11.668 --> 20:13.295
This is really awkward, you know?

20:13.378 --> 20:15.714
Really? I feel fine, though.

20:16.715 --> 20:19.051
- Really?
- Mm-hm. I'm totally fine.

20:19.676 --> 20:21.553
Why on earth would we be awkward?

20:22.054 --> 20:25.349
Hmm. You must have decided
to pretend not to remember.

20:25.849 --> 20:28.227
- I don't know what you're saying.
- Hey, Kook Yeon-su.

20:31.355 --> 20:33.315
All right, fine. It's awkward.

20:33.398 --> 20:35.234
I got drunk and cried in front of my ex.

20:35.317 --> 20:37.194
So I'm embarrassed. Happy now?

20:38.070 --> 20:39.571
Uh…

20:43.742 --> 20:46.370
Like I said, for me running away
is not avoidance 

20:46.453 --> 20:47.788
but a reasonable decision.

20:50.958 --> 20:52.209
So sometimes…

20:53.377 --> 20:55.045
I don't make that decision.

20:57.506 --> 20:59.049
You wanna grab a bite?

21:16.817 --> 21:19.111
EXCESSIVE LIFE
BEGINNING A JOURNEY

21:25.575 --> 21:29.955
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

21:34.001 --> 21:35.544
- Here.
- Thank you.

21:38.088 --> 21:39.798
I don't know
what it is that you're thinking.

21:39.881 --> 21:42.509
If you don't wanna do this,
you can say no.

21:42.592 --> 21:43.635
It's volunteer work.

21:44.928 --> 21:46.763
You're not that warm-hearted, are you?

21:47.264 --> 21:48.974
This isn't helping you at all.

21:51.560 --> 21:54.187
Miss NJ, please have this.
I got it for you.

21:54.855 --> 21:56.189
You didn't have to, but thank you.

21:56.273 --> 21:59.192
Miss NJ, you look
more beautiful in person.

21:59.276 --> 22:01.111
Thank you very much.

22:06.033 --> 22:07.284
Where's your pride?

22:08.201 --> 22:12.080
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

22:12.164 --> 22:13.582
You all came here

22:13.665 --> 22:17.044
because NJ will drop the charges
if you do this, right?

22:17.127 --> 22:21.006
Yeah. I heard everyone who came
to do this were let off last year.

22:21.089 --> 22:23.008
That's right, she'll drop the charges.

22:23.091 --> 22:24.092
How do you know?

22:24.176 --> 22:27.387
Well, actually the truth is,
I came here last year too.

22:27.471 --> 22:28.847
Oh, gosh.

22:28.930 --> 22:30.724
Are you saying you got caught again?

22:30.807 --> 22:32.768
Well, I just had really bad luck.

22:32.851 --> 22:36.021
Honestly, they say everything
is a malicious comment these days.

22:36.104 --> 22:40.609
I guess so. To be honest,
don't you think this is ridiculous?

22:40.692 --> 22:43.612
Volunteer work with people
who wrote bad comments about her?

22:43.695 --> 22:47.032
I don't know if she has
really high self-esteem or if she's smart.

22:47.115 --> 22:49.242
It's all for her image, of course.

22:49.326 --> 22:50.660
She's a tough one, you know.

22:51.328 --> 22:54.247
Anyway, just keep sucking up to her
and she'll let you off.

22:54.331 --> 22:56.875
Hang in there until it's over.

22:56.958 --> 23:00.379
By the way, did you see those stickers
on the lunch boxes?

23:00.462 --> 23:03.465
There's no way anyone here
would ever want to see her stupid face,

23:03.548 --> 23:05.342
especially while they're eating.

23:05.425 --> 23:07.427
- I tore it off already.
- Oh.

23:07.511 --> 23:10.555
She's so young, but she's as sly as a fox.

23:10.639 --> 23:12.974
Hold on, what kind of comment
did you write?

23:13.058 --> 23:15.852
Oh, please. I didn't even
make up any stories about her.

23:16.436 --> 23:18.021
You know, there was something…

23:19.398 --> 23:22.943
there was a rumor
about NJ and her sponsors.

23:23.026 --> 23:24.861
And I just wrote about that a bit.

23:24.945 --> 23:27.781
Hold on, NJ even had sponsors?

23:27.864 --> 23:29.741
No way! Since when?

23:31.076 --> 23:36.206
Her agency is willing going after
innocent citizens like us to keep quiet.

23:36.289 --> 23:37.457
I know, right?

23:37.541 --> 23:40.710
Remember when her first album
went viral right after her debut?

23:40.794 --> 23:44.214
I heard her sponsors got her
all those commercials back then.

23:44.297 --> 23:47.634
That's how she bought
all those expensive buildings at her age.

23:47.717 --> 23:49.010
That's crazy.

24:00.897 --> 24:02.274
Come on. It's this way.

24:09.281 --> 24:10.699
WITH UNG

24:12.993 --> 24:15.620
Ung, what have you been doing all day?

24:16.288 --> 24:17.247
Good day to you.

24:19.249 --> 24:20.500
Oh, it's Yeon-su!

24:20.584 --> 24:21.710
Yeon-su's here!

24:21.793 --> 24:25.547
Oh, my goodness! Yeon-su!

24:25.630 --> 24:28.842
Oh, I'm so glad you're here, Yeon-su.

24:28.925 --> 24:30.594
- Are you here to eat?
- Yes.

24:31.261 --> 24:32.345
Oh. Sit over there.

24:33.138 --> 24:35.557
Were you able to get home safe last night?

24:35.640 --> 24:39.144
- Of course. Please have a seat here.
- Can you even see me, Mom?

24:41.438 --> 24:43.190
- It's been such a long time.
- Yes.

24:43.273 --> 24:45.692
What would you like, Yeon-su?
I'll cook anything for you.

24:45.775 --> 24:48.987
Oh, no. Anything is fine.
Everything you make is so delicious.

24:49.070 --> 24:52.365
But still. Is there anything
you're craving for?

24:52.449 --> 24:56.661
Well, do you still happen
to make that bean stew?

24:56.745 --> 25:00.040
Of course!
You used to love that, didn't you?

25:00.582 --> 25:01.958
I'll make some right away.

25:02.042 --> 25:03.752
- Thank you.
- Hey, Mom, I want--

25:03.835 --> 25:06.671
I'll get you some meat and some other
side dishes. Eat all you want, okay?

25:06.755 --> 25:08.507
- Thank you.
- Ho, I'm here.

25:09.174 --> 25:11.468
Weren't you here just a minute ago?

25:12.719 --> 25:14.846
Oh. When did Ung get here?

25:14.930 --> 25:16.723
Oh, hang on.

25:16.806 --> 25:18.934
- Go.
- But, wait. Ji-ung…

25:19.518 --> 25:22.312
Ji-ung asked me to call him
if I ever saw Ung.

25:22.395 --> 25:25.065
All right. But don't call him, okay?
Just go away.

25:25.148 --> 25:26.942
Ji-ung was looking
everywhere for him.

25:27.526 --> 25:28.777
Just go. Go!

25:38.370 --> 25:40.455
Would looking through that
give you an answer?

25:40.539 --> 25:44.042
I'm pretty sure I told you
I don't like the smell of food in here.

25:44.125 --> 25:46.127
I'm done eating. You're so sensitive.

25:47.462 --> 25:48.463
So did you eat?

25:49.297 --> 25:50.173
Yes, I ate.

25:51.174 --> 25:52.884
Outside the editing room.

25:54.344 --> 25:57.430
Hey, I heard they ran away.

25:58.348 --> 26:02.102
You know, I'm surprised it took them
this long before they ran away.

26:02.936 --> 26:06.022
- They haven't changed a single bit, huh.
- You mean you knew?

26:06.731 --> 26:10.110
They ran away for about two weeks
when we filmed ten years ago.

26:10.193 --> 26:12.404
You didn't know?

26:12.487 --> 26:14.656
The day Yeon-su went home,
and Ung was absent?

26:14.739 --> 26:16.074
That's right.

26:16.157 --> 26:19.035
They both disappeared without a word,
so we looked everywhere just to find them.

26:19.119 --> 26:21.746
- So where'd you end up finding them?
- We didn't find them.

26:22.372 --> 26:25.000
But they seemed to have
reached an agreement.

26:25.083 --> 26:27.419
They just returned
as if nothing happened at all.

26:27.919 --> 26:29.504
- What? Seriously?
- It's obvious.

26:29.588 --> 26:31.840
They'll return
by themselves sooner or later,

26:31.923 --> 26:33.466
so just wait a bit before you swoop in.

26:33.550 --> 26:35.093
Don't worry about it so much.

26:36.011 --> 26:39.514
Hey, I hear Chae-ran was looking
for some lodging. Are you going somewhere?

26:39.598 --> 26:40.807
Can I join you guys?

26:40.890 --> 26:43.143
We are not going out to have fun.

26:43.226 --> 26:45.228
Ms. Lee wanted to come too,
but I turned her down.

26:45.312 --> 26:48.440
So don't even think about it.
Please grow up, the both of you.

26:53.987 --> 26:57.073
I was able to compile a list
of places we can go to.

26:57.157 --> 26:59.075
Should we decide on one
after we find them?

26:59.159 --> 27:00.452
No, prepare it in advance.

27:00.535 --> 27:03.204
We won't have enough time afterward.

27:03.288 --> 27:06.875
In any case, I'll make sure
to get them today, no matter what.

27:10.503 --> 27:11.338
Is he useful?

27:11.421 --> 27:13.298
I told him to make a list of lodgings,

27:13.381 --> 27:17.093
and he gave me about 20 pages of places
where newlyweds would go.

27:17.177 --> 27:19.554
He's obviously good at organizing stuff.

27:19.638 --> 27:21.765
I already feel nauseous about it.

27:21.848 --> 27:23.058
He's so different from me.

27:24.809 --> 27:26.227
Mr. Kim!

27:26.311 --> 27:28.313
Going out on business?
I can drive you there, sir.

27:28.396 --> 27:29.689
No, it's fine.

27:30.607 --> 27:31.608
Oh, hey, Intern. You can--

27:31.691 --> 27:33.276
- You can--
- Im Tae-hun, that's my name.

27:33.360 --> 27:35.487
Okay, Intern. Why don't you--

27:35.570 --> 27:37.197
Im Tae-hun, sir.

27:41.618 --> 27:43.453
Okay, Imtern,
I'm calling you that from now on.

27:43.536 --> 27:46.665
Imtern, you go home.
Go and pack your things. Okay?

27:46.748 --> 27:48.083
Okay.

27:48.166 --> 27:49.959
- Chae-ran, wrap up here.
- Yes.

27:52.170 --> 27:53.838
- Imtern.
- Sir.

28:15.068 --> 28:17.070
Are you uncomfortable here?

28:18.071 --> 28:20.615
Uh, no, I was thinking
of visiting soon anyway.

28:21.574 --> 28:25.120
Uh, your parents seem
rather healthy today. I'm happy.

28:26.413 --> 28:29.332
Yeah. They have aged quite a lot, though.

28:31.042 --> 28:33.211
Your grandma? Is she doing all right?

28:33.878 --> 28:35.797
Mm-hm, she's good.

28:35.880 --> 28:37.298
Hm.

28:42.470 --> 28:44.723
- What are they saying?
- I don't know.

28:44.806 --> 28:46.224
- Okay, give me that.
- Here.

28:46.307 --> 28:48.101
Wow, these radishes are really…

28:48.184 --> 28:49.978
You didn't answer my question yet.

28:53.606 --> 28:54.941
Come here.

28:58.319 --> 28:59.904
How have you been doing lately?

29:02.323 --> 29:05.493
Well, I, I just graduated and worked.

29:06.661 --> 29:07.579
Yeah.

29:08.496 --> 29:09.456
I did okay.

29:11.958 --> 29:12.834
Is that it?

29:13.668 --> 29:16.045
Mm-hm. It's nothing special.

29:17.797 --> 29:19.924
- Then yesterday was--
- Yesterday…

29:20.008 --> 29:21.843
I was just really drunk yesterday.

29:22.719 --> 29:25.096
It's embarrassing, so forget it.

29:25.180 --> 29:27.557
You know it was
because I was feeling stressed

29:27.640 --> 29:29.768
about this project that I was working on.

29:37.525 --> 29:38.943
I enjoyed the food.

29:40.528 --> 29:41.571
I should get going.

29:44.699 --> 29:47.243
Wait, Yeon-su,
why are you leaving so soon?

29:47.327 --> 29:48.203
- Oh, gosh.
- Oh, uh,

29:48.286 --> 29:49.704
I really enjoyed the food you made.

29:49.788 --> 29:52.957
But I didn't expect to come here,
so I didn't bring anything.

29:53.041 --> 29:54.876
Oh, dear, there's no need for that.

29:54.959 --> 29:58.338
You can come visit us
any time you like, all right?

29:58.421 --> 30:00.757
- Okay.
- Oh, wait. Hang on.

30:00.840 --> 30:02.634
- I packed some side dishes for you.
- Wait here.

30:02.717 --> 30:04.427
- No, it's fine.
- No, no. Give them to her.

30:04.511 --> 30:06.304
Here you go,
eat them with your grandmother.

30:07.180 --> 30:10.391
If you can, maybe next time
you can bring her along with you.

30:10.475 --> 30:12.018
There's really no need.

30:13.061 --> 30:15.563
But I'll be sure to enjoy these.
Thank you very much.

30:15.647 --> 30:16.773
- Come back again.
- Ung.

30:17.649 --> 30:19.776
- Take her home.
- It's okay. I can go by myself.

30:19.859 --> 30:21.528
- No, no, no. Go on.
- Of course not!

30:22.946 --> 30:25.949
- Come back soon, bye.
- Okay.

30:26.616 --> 30:28.034
You get home safely.

30:29.994 --> 30:31.246
- Bye.
- Bye.

30:38.378 --> 30:39.879
How do they seem to you?

30:40.880 --> 30:42.924
Honestly, I don't have a single clue.

30:51.933 --> 30:53.309
I used to say this to you,

30:53.393 --> 30:56.688
you should be good to your parents.
They're always so kind and nice.

30:59.858 --> 31:00.984
Are you going home?

31:01.818 --> 31:04.696
I don't suppose Ji-ung will still
be waiting there, will he?

31:06.030 --> 31:08.741
We both went AWOL
without telling any of them,

31:08.825 --> 31:10.869
so let's apologize
and start filming again…

31:11.619 --> 31:13.872
Right. It was this feeling.

31:15.665 --> 31:17.667
This is how I felt while dating you.

31:19.460 --> 31:21.254
I was like an idiot waiting for you,

31:22.255 --> 31:24.716
always watching you walk away,
step by step.

31:25.383 --> 31:26.509
That's how it was.

31:28.428 --> 31:30.346
What? What do you mean?

31:30.930 --> 31:33.433
Whenever you said you were okay,
I had to accept it.

31:34.934 --> 31:36.352
When you said nothing was wrong,

31:37.270 --> 31:39.105
I had to say I worried for no reason.

31:40.356 --> 31:41.858
When you wanted to break up,

31:42.817 --> 31:45.570
I had to accept without knowing why.

31:46.654 --> 31:48.615
And when I finally met you again,

31:49.908 --> 31:51.743
I had no idea how you'd be doing…

31:53.870 --> 31:56.456
or whatever it was that
you were thinking about at that time…

31:59.334 --> 32:02.754
but I had to just accept things.

32:02.837 --> 32:05.131
"The best defense
is a good offense."

32:06.174 --> 32:08.676
It really feels like you're back, Yeon-su.

32:10.845 --> 32:12.096
Choi Ung.

32:12.180 --> 32:14.307
I'm really sick of this.

32:16.517 --> 32:18.561
I guess I'm doing that right now.

32:21.940 --> 32:25.276
But this was not my choice at all.

32:47.215 --> 32:49.550
One, two, three!

32:50.468 --> 32:51.636
Good job.

32:51.719 --> 32:53.304
Good job!

32:53.972 --> 32:55.890
- Good job.
- Good job, everyone.

32:55.974 --> 32:57.392
Miss NJ.

32:58.434 --> 33:01.688
Thanks to you, I, uh, had
a really meaningful experience today.

33:01.771 --> 33:02.897
Thank you.

33:04.065 --> 33:08.319
Thanks to today, we were able
to reflect on ourselves and our actions.

33:08.403 --> 33:11.280
Thank you so much
for giving us this opportunity.

33:11.364 --> 33:13.491
This means
you're going to let us off, right?

33:13.574 --> 33:14.826
Jeez.

33:15.660 --> 33:18.871
We promise that we will do our best
to make up for our mistakes.

33:18.955 --> 33:23.001
And also, we'll tell everyone
we know about how cool you were today.

33:23.084 --> 33:24.669
Okay?

33:26.963 --> 33:29.173
Sure. All right.

33:32.427 --> 33:34.262
- Hey, Director.
- Yes?

33:34.345 --> 33:37.098
I'm sorry,
but I can't come here anymore.

33:37.181 --> 33:38.016
And why not?

33:38.099 --> 33:40.184
I thought they would end
after a few times.

33:40.268 --> 33:42.854
I didn't think there would be
an endless line of trolls.

33:44.647 --> 33:45.815
They're not my fans at all.

33:46.983 --> 33:48.985
They're the internet trolls I sued.

33:49.068 --> 33:50.653
- Hey, NJ.
- What?

33:50.737 --> 33:52.321
Who? Me?

33:53.031 --> 33:56.826
Oh, well, you always seemed
to call me a bitch, didn't you?

33:59.579 --> 34:02.206
I'm not dropping the charges.

34:02.290 --> 34:03.624
Good work today, everyone.

34:04.500 --> 34:06.627
Thank you for joining me
when I asked you all

34:06.711 --> 34:08.504
if you wanted to do some volunteer work.

34:08.588 --> 34:10.048
Get home safely.

34:10.131 --> 34:12.550
- But…
- Wait a second. You can't just do this!

34:12.633 --> 34:15.595
It's not fair. This is such a scam.

34:16.262 --> 34:19.891
You said you'd drop the charges
against us. This is so ridiculous.

34:22.560 --> 34:26.439
Did I? I don't think
I ever promised to drop the charges.

34:27.857 --> 34:29.984
You ate with me here last year, right?

34:30.068 --> 34:32.278
Did you troll me
because you wanted to see me again?

34:32.361 --> 34:33.821
Well, that was…

34:35.239 --> 34:38.201
Can't I even criticize you?
Is it all trolling to you?

34:41.079 --> 34:44.665
Should I read the comments
you wrote about me to everyone here then?

34:45.500 --> 34:48.044
Let's see if it's criticism
or just trolling.

34:48.127 --> 34:49.420
- Hey, wait.
- What?

34:49.504 --> 34:52.924
You're just abusing the power you have
against the innocent citizens.

34:53.007 --> 34:54.467
We're all busy people, you know.

34:54.550 --> 34:56.677
You were just making us
waste our time here!

34:57.762 --> 35:00.348
You'd better suck up to me
if you at least want a lower sentence.

35:01.641 --> 35:02.767
Are you sure about this?

35:08.731 --> 35:09.732
Miss NJ.

35:10.233 --> 35:14.153
As you know, uh,
I only made this mistake once.

35:14.737 --> 35:18.574
If I get charged for this,
I'll have a hard time getting a job.

35:18.658 --> 35:22.245
My life is at stake here.
Can you please let me off this time?

35:25.832 --> 35:28.876
All right. After all,
you only did it once, right?

35:30.253 --> 35:31.796
So I'll only sue you just once.

35:32.588 --> 35:34.757
And if you do it twice,
then I'll sue you twice.

35:35.925 --> 35:40.304
Hey, people can make mistakes sometimes.

35:40.388 --> 35:41.889
Do you have to be so cruel
because of that?

35:41.973 --> 35:45.476
How can you write sexually harassing
comments with such detail by mistake?

35:45.560 --> 35:47.145
Your ID is Bibibik, right?

35:47.937 --> 35:49.897
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

35:51.065 --> 35:53.276
There were articles
about how this was a place

35:53.359 --> 35:55.194
for reconciliation and forgiveness.

35:55.278 --> 35:57.238
Go and tell people that it isn't.

35:57.321 --> 36:00.158
Go ahead and tell everyone
that I'm just a crazy bitch

36:00.241 --> 36:01.784
who was bent on suing you.

36:01.868 --> 36:04.162
And I was acting unlike myself.

36:06.247 --> 36:07.456
Tell them all…

36:08.791 --> 36:10.084
like you always do.

36:15.673 --> 36:17.216
Can't believe her.

36:23.264 --> 36:24.682
Damn it.

36:26.017 --> 36:27.560
Why did I say that?

36:27.643 --> 36:31.689
I just wanted to go back home
and sleep all day.

36:37.695 --> 36:39.071
WHY DID YOU TWO SUDDENLY GO AWOL?

36:41.699 --> 36:43.868
- Choi Ung!
- Choi Ung!

36:43.951 --> 36:45.828
Congratulations!

36:45.912 --> 36:48.122
We know that you're far away right now,

36:48.206 --> 36:50.041
but we're still congratulating you.

36:50.124 --> 36:51.709
Super punch!

36:51.792 --> 36:54.253
You said you liked
how happy you are in this picture.

36:54.337 --> 36:57.381
Right? You're happy, aren't you?
Why don't you smile, huh?

36:57.465 --> 37:00.551
Hey, I heard you're earning a fortune.

37:00.635 --> 37:03.179
Maybe you can buy my bar? Please, Ung?

37:03.262 --> 37:07.016
Ung, you and I have finally succeeded.

37:07.099 --> 37:11.187
I can't believe that the dim-witted Ung
has succeeded this much.

37:11.270 --> 37:12.605
I'm so proud of you!

37:12.688 --> 37:14.232
I just feel so…

37:14.982 --> 37:18.319
I… I still can't believe… I…

37:18.402 --> 37:22.073
got to see my idiot friend succeed…

37:22.156 --> 37:25.243
Oh, no, I'm going to start crying too!

37:25.326 --> 37:27.703
He didn't even
get to eat properly…

37:27.787 --> 37:29.330
Oh! Don't cry.

37:29.413 --> 37:32.375
He suffered so much, you know that?

37:32.458 --> 37:33.459
Hey!

37:33.960 --> 37:37.964
You have to be happy, you understand?
You got that, huh?

37:40.675 --> 37:43.219
It looks more
like they're holding my funeral.

37:44.845 --> 37:46.222
Should I report them?

37:47.139 --> 37:49.267
Eun-ho's an ass.

37:49.350 --> 37:50.601
Huh?

37:50.685 --> 37:52.311
NJ

37:59.527 --> 38:00.820
It was this feeling.

38:01.487 --> 38:03.614
I was like an idiot waiting for you,

38:03.698 --> 38:06.409
always watching you walk away,
step by step.

38:07.118 --> 38:08.286
That's how it was.

38:09.203 --> 38:11.205
I'm really sick of this.

38:11.289 --> 38:12.498
Yeon-su?

38:17.378 --> 38:19.880
Hey, why are you standing there?

38:19.964 --> 38:22.174
- Did you just get here?
- Oh.

38:23.342 --> 38:25.136
What's that in your hand?

38:30.766 --> 38:33.019
Uh, Grandma, I'll be back
in a moment, okay?

38:33.102 --> 38:35.021
Wait, didn't you just get home?

38:37.857 --> 38:40.151
You should have
just done that a long time ago.

38:40.234 --> 38:42.028
It's not something you can forgive easily.

38:42.111 --> 38:44.989
"The angelic NJ
who forgives her online haters"?

38:45.072 --> 38:46.407
To hell with that nonsense.

38:46.490 --> 38:49.952
Tell our agency that you won't be
dropping charges for anyone anymore.

38:50.786 --> 38:52.330
What a bunch of jerks.

38:53.414 --> 38:54.498
Hey…

38:55.374 --> 38:56.417
what's gotten into you?

38:56.500 --> 38:58.586
Why did you wanna
meet them in person anyway?

38:59.378 --> 39:00.546
I thought…

39:02.089 --> 39:04.967
it'd be less scary
if I saw the real people behind it all.

39:06.469 --> 39:08.804
Just avoid them. Run away.

39:09.972 --> 39:11.140
It's okay.

39:19.398 --> 39:21.359
That's why I'm running away this time.

39:23.444 --> 39:24.820
Where? To that guy again?

39:29.909 --> 39:30.910
Yes.

39:33.579 --> 39:34.872
Choi Ung!

39:36.040 --> 39:37.208
Oh.

39:37.708 --> 39:39.210
Oh.

39:40.252 --> 39:43.339
Oh…

39:43.923 --> 39:45.883
I guess I called at the perfect time.

39:46.842 --> 39:49.929
Tell me, were you wandering around
after running away from home?

39:50.012 --> 39:52.014
Please, running away at this age?

39:52.098 --> 39:53.391
I was…

39:54.100 --> 39:56.560
…just trying to have some time
for myself, that's all.

39:56.644 --> 39:59.146
If you don't want
to do the documentary, don't.

39:59.230 --> 40:03.109
It'd be quite overwhelming for someone
who isn't a celebrity.

40:13.411 --> 40:14.954
It's okay. Come here.

40:15.454 --> 40:17.415
You can bring those bags too.

40:23.712 --> 40:26.882
Wow, no way! NJ?

40:26.966 --> 40:29.093
You're the NJ? Really?

40:29.176 --> 40:31.137
Mm-hm. Do you have a pen?

40:31.220 --> 40:32.221
Oh.

40:39.395 --> 40:43.607
Hey, kid. You should ask permission first
before taking photos of someone.

40:43.691 --> 40:44.942
Can I please take a photo?

40:45.025 --> 40:46.402
No, you can't.

40:46.485 --> 40:49.196
There are lots
of pretty photos online.

40:49.905 --> 40:51.073
- Wow.
- Here.

40:51.699 --> 40:53.826
Do you kids know what scarcity is?

40:54.618 --> 40:55.661
What about rare items?

40:55.744 --> 40:57.163
- Yes.
- Yes.

40:57.872 --> 41:00.374
If you want your bags
to become rare items,

41:00.458 --> 41:04.420
you shouldn't tell anyone that I was here
or that you saw me here. You got that?

41:05.087 --> 41:06.297
- Okay.
- Okay.

41:06.380 --> 41:08.174
If you tell people I'm here,

41:08.257 --> 41:11.051
I'll end up signing
every single person's bags.

41:11.886 --> 41:13.762
- So you shouldn't?
- Yes.

41:13.846 --> 41:15.890
Run along now. I'm talking to my friend.

41:16.474 --> 41:18.100
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you very much.

41:23.147 --> 41:25.691
Even little kids recognize you, huh?

41:26.275 --> 41:27.693
It must be tiring, though.

41:28.611 --> 41:31.280
Regular citizens like you
don't know what it's like.

41:32.490 --> 41:35.868
Wait. I think you should understand
a bit about it by now.

41:37.328 --> 41:40.164
Well, there were some who did recognize me

41:40.247 --> 41:42.666
only because of that stupid documentary.

41:42.750 --> 41:44.668
Then why are you filming it again?

41:45.461 --> 41:47.296
I don't know. It just sort of happened.

41:47.796 --> 41:50.716
I've fallen into my own trap, I guess.

41:50.799 --> 41:53.636
Well, that happens sometimes.

42:04.146 --> 42:05.981
Did you really just laugh at me?

42:06.982 --> 42:08.984
Let's eat lunch together.

42:09.068 --> 42:12.029
Oh, sorry but I just ate.

42:15.199 --> 42:20.079
Mr. Choi. I really didn't want to say
this sort of thing to you myself, but…

42:20.621 --> 42:22.289
I'm actually a type A.

42:22.373 --> 42:25.000
My Myers Briggs is actually ISFP,

42:25.084 --> 42:28.045
so I'm introverted and sensitive
even though I don't seem like it.

42:28.128 --> 42:30.756
That's why I wrote some things down
in my heart diary earlier.

42:31.674 --> 42:32.967
A what diary?

42:33.050 --> 42:33.926
First of all.

42:34.552 --> 42:37.012
"Mr. Choi got famous
because I bought one of his works,

42:37.096 --> 42:39.640
but why doesn't he want to buy me a meal?"

42:39.723 --> 42:40.766
Secondly.

42:40.849 --> 42:42.393
"I asked him to draw my buildings,

42:42.476 --> 42:45.187
but why is that he doesn't want
to contact me even one?"

42:45.938 --> 42:47.398
And thirdly.

42:47.481 --> 42:49.149
"I made him even more popular

42:49.233 --> 42:52.403
by going to his drawing show
when I wasn't even invited,

42:52.486 --> 42:55.447
but why hasn't he asked me out
still until now?"

42:55.531 --> 42:56.490
Well, I--

42:56.574 --> 42:59.285
Those are the three debts that
you have with me right now.

42:59.368 --> 43:00.911
So how will you pay me that?

43:13.507 --> 43:16.760
Does he think he's the only one
who can get upset? Unbelievable.

43:17.344 --> 43:19.722
When did he ever tell me anything anyway?

43:19.805 --> 43:22.850
Choi Ung was always the one who hid…

43:22.933 --> 43:24.977
Why the hell isn't he picking up?

43:25.060 --> 43:26.770
…whenever he was upset.

43:32.943 --> 43:36.155
Oh, I think…

43:38.324 --> 43:41.160
This is something that I didn't expect.

43:42.620 --> 43:43.746
Yeon-su.

43:48.000 --> 43:49.001
Uh…

43:50.461 --> 43:51.337
Oh.

43:52.379 --> 43:56.258
Seriously,
why are you always so clumsy?

43:57.635 --> 44:00.846
Anyway, I thought everyone
would pretend not to have eaten

44:00.929 --> 44:02.765
if I asked to have a meal together.

44:03.265 --> 44:04.975
You're so difficult to deal with.

44:06.685 --> 44:08.979
Uh, well, NJ, um…

44:09.063 --> 44:12.691
I notice that you always gotten
in touch with me like this.

44:13.400 --> 44:15.361
And you just keep on popping up.

44:17.154 --> 44:20.115
I've been pretty clueless, haven't I?

44:22.117 --> 44:25.245
But weren't you pretending to be clueless?

44:25.329 --> 44:26.914
Oh, I guess that's true…

44:29.041 --> 44:31.418
I'm sorry. I guess
I should have mentioned it first.

44:31.502 --> 44:33.045
My point, exactly.

44:33.754 --> 44:36.090
It's way too embarrassing
for me to say it myself.

44:38.050 --> 44:39.134
Well…

44:42.805 --> 44:45.391
Since you bought three drawings,
I'll give you one for free.

44:45.474 --> 44:47.976
Look, I don't usually do this,
but I'll make an exception

44:48.060 --> 44:50.813
- since you're NJ, if there's anything--
- Hold on a minute, Mr. Choi.

44:50.896 --> 44:52.439
I have a lot of money.

44:52.523 --> 44:55.776
Do you think really I'm doing this
just to get a free drawing?

44:56.402 --> 44:59.738
Huh? Then why are you being so nice to me?

45:00.781 --> 45:02.825
Do I need a reason?

45:02.908 --> 45:04.910
No, that's not what I mean.

45:04.993 --> 45:07.413
- I meant that I don't get why you would--
- Because I like you.

45:07.496 --> 45:08.372
Huh?

45:09.248 --> 45:11.041
Oh!

45:11.125 --> 45:14.211
Oh, no, why do you make such a mess?

45:15.129 --> 45:16.338
What do…

45:18.215 --> 45:20.801
I just had a really tough day today.

45:21.427 --> 45:25.180
I didn't want to whine about it to you
because it's a pretty normal thing for me.

45:26.515 --> 45:27.850
But then…

45:28.434 --> 45:30.728
I always feel better
whenever I see you.

45:31.729 --> 45:34.106
At first, I felt better
when I saw your drawings.

45:34.857 --> 45:36.817
But now, I feel it with you too.

45:37.985 --> 45:41.113
And that is my reason
for coming to see you.

45:42.114 --> 45:44.533
So stop getting so startled
whenever you see me.

45:45.200 --> 45:46.744
And don't always look so shocked either.

45:47.661 --> 45:51.039
I'm not saying I love you, nor that
it means that I'm asking you out.

45:51.123 --> 45:54.126
All I'm saying is that I like you.

45:54.209 --> 45:57.838
Maybe it's because
you kind of look like my Tofu.

45:59.506 --> 46:00.758
"Tofu"?

46:00.841 --> 46:02.426
Mm. My pet dog.

46:03.719 --> 46:04.887
Oh, your dog.

46:09.141 --> 46:10.934
Are you going somewhere?

46:11.018 --> 46:13.729
Sometimes there are kids
who just don't listen.

46:14.605 --> 46:16.690
I should get going.
Let's hang out again some time.

46:17.566 --> 46:19.401
You should go home too while you can.

46:26.909 --> 46:29.244
They're back again.

46:37.711 --> 46:39.296
You're so unbelievable.

46:39.379 --> 46:41.006
Were you looking for me all day?

46:41.089 --> 46:43.592
No, I just started looking for you.

46:43.675 --> 46:45.761
And I just so happened
to get lucky and bump into you.

46:45.844 --> 46:47.471
I didn't even have to go very far.

46:48.305 --> 46:50.766
- So what were you doing?
- Oh, walking.

46:59.691 --> 47:00.567
Okay.

47:01.235 --> 47:02.945
Then why did you run away today?

47:03.946 --> 47:05.197
I just needed a break.

47:05.906 --> 47:07.074
You just needed a break?

47:07.157 --> 47:10.953
Mm, yeah. I just wanted to feel
some freedom today. That's all.

47:11.036 --> 47:14.122
Is that so? You should have told me then.
You'll be free from us very soon.

47:14.206 --> 47:16.291
- What?
- Nothing. Never mind that.

47:17.417 --> 47:19.044
Are you still gonna be in it?

47:21.505 --> 47:23.507
I'm just confirming. Don't answer that.

47:23.590 --> 47:24.675
- Hey.
- Sorry.

47:28.804 --> 47:30.264
Did you fight with Ung again?

47:30.347 --> 47:34.184
No, not really.
He just got angry with me. That's all.

47:34.268 --> 47:36.603
When on earth did he become
so short-tempered?

47:37.312 --> 47:38.480
When do you think?

47:42.943 --> 47:44.778
Fine. Everything's my fault.

47:44.862 --> 47:48.031
Well, I wouldn't say everything.
Maybe about half.

47:48.115 --> 47:49.908
It's around half and half with Ung.

47:49.992 --> 47:50.993
It's half?

47:51.743 --> 47:54.788
Breaking up isn't usually
just one person's fault.

47:54.872 --> 47:56.248
It's the same for both sides.

48:01.962 --> 48:04.131
What is it? Something wrong?

48:04.214 --> 48:06.383
You seem to know a lot about dating.

48:07.467 --> 48:08.510
What?

48:08.594 --> 48:10.512
Tell me, are you seeing someone?

48:11.889 --> 48:13.348
Gosh.

48:14.474 --> 48:16.059
Guess you're not.

48:16.143 --> 48:17.436
Have you ever dated before?

48:17.519 --> 48:20.814
Yeon-su. You see, there are
two kinds of men in this world.

48:20.898 --> 48:22.816
Men who can't date,
and men who don't date.

48:22.900 --> 48:24.651
So you're a guy who can't date.

48:27.195 --> 48:28.405
What? You're so ridiculous.

48:28.488 --> 48:31.783
I think that you'd be shocked to find out
just the kind of person I really am.

48:31.867 --> 48:33.660
Really? What kind of person are you?

48:35.037 --> 48:36.997
Well, I'm the bad boy type.

48:38.540 --> 48:40.125
You know what a homme fatale is, right?

48:40.208 --> 48:43.629
The "fatale" means the attraction
could be fatal to women. That's me.

48:43.712 --> 48:47.049
That's why I try to keep my attractiveness
hidden so I won't harm others.

48:47.132 --> 48:49.134
Oh, Kim Ji-ung.

48:49.217 --> 48:51.595
When did you become so shameless, huh?

48:52.304 --> 48:53.680
You're so funny.

48:54.932 --> 48:57.017
That wasn't a joke, you know. I'm serious.

48:57.100 --> 49:01.146
Yeah, but you were a bit popular
when we were in high school, remember?

49:01.229 --> 49:02.356
You finally get me.

49:02.439 --> 49:03.440
But why, though?

49:04.274 --> 49:06.151
Hey, that's kind of mean, you know.

49:06.234 --> 49:08.737
I guess it helped that
you were the student president.

49:09.738 --> 49:11.615
You just didn't know me much back then.

49:16.662 --> 49:18.288
I'm getting drunk.

49:20.874 --> 49:22.376
That idiot.

49:23.210 --> 49:25.545
Is that Sol-i?

49:25.629 --> 49:27.839
She's the finale of my terrible day.

49:28.674 --> 49:29.716
Sol-i!

49:29.800 --> 49:31.301
Sol-i.

49:31.385 --> 49:32.552
Sol-i!

49:33.470 --> 49:34.972
Kook Yeon-su!

49:38.976 --> 49:40.143
What's all this?

49:40.227 --> 49:42.062
- I'm drunk.
- Wow.

49:52.990 --> 49:54.074
Eun-ho?

50:04.292 --> 50:06.253
Are you finally dead?

50:19.558 --> 50:21.268
I know this isn't a raise,

50:21.351 --> 50:23.687
but you're better off gone
than getting one.

50:26.106 --> 50:28.316
You made a total mess in here.

50:30.068 --> 50:32.112
I'm going to puke.

50:33.113 --> 50:36.033
- You're so unbelievable.
- Oh, I'm going to puke.

50:36.950 --> 50:39.036
You're such a pain, you know?

50:41.329 --> 50:43.081
Is it really okay for her
to sleep in here?

50:43.165 --> 50:44.332
Her dad's a minister.

50:44.416 --> 50:46.752
Believe it or not,
her family's very religious.

50:46.835 --> 50:48.420
They don't know that she actually drinks.

50:48.503 --> 50:49.880
I love you, God.

50:50.714 --> 50:53.050
How do they not know
that she's running a bar?

50:53.133 --> 50:54.968
Well, you should really see
her act some time.

50:55.052 --> 50:57.429
She should have been an actress,
not a writer.

50:58.221 --> 51:01.141
- I love you, sachangnim.
- No, go to sleep.

51:01.224 --> 51:03.602
I'm sorry you got dragged into this.

51:04.102 --> 51:06.980
- What's going on here?
- Grandma!

51:07.064 --> 51:10.901
Oh, good Lord. Aren't you Ji-ung? Oh, my.

51:10.984 --> 51:13.487
- It's so nice to see you.
- How have you been?

51:13.570 --> 51:15.238
It looks like you got so much younger.

51:15.322 --> 51:17.157
Oh, come on.

51:17.240 --> 51:18.200
- How are you?
- Hold it.

51:18.283 --> 51:19.910
Since when were you two so close, huh?

51:19.993 --> 51:23.538
Oh, don't you know?
Ji-ung's the sweetest boy I've ever met.

51:24.623 --> 51:25.749
Have you eaten, Ung?

51:25.832 --> 51:27.793
- How about something to eat, huh?
- All right.

51:27.876 --> 51:30.670
What the hell is that stench?

51:33.298 --> 51:35.717
Oh, that little brat!
Is that troublemaker drunk again?

51:35.801 --> 51:37.260
- Please, can you leave my room now?
- Where did you go

51:37.344 --> 51:38.386
- to get plastered like that?
- Go on. Go.

51:38.470 --> 51:40.597
Oh, goodness this girl.

51:43.809 --> 51:45.435
Welcome!

51:59.407 --> 52:02.327
Ung! My Ung who ran away.

52:02.828 --> 52:05.330
I knew you'd be successful one day.

52:06.039 --> 52:08.708
I'm so proud of what you've become.

52:09.584 --> 52:11.753
I'm still not forgiving you.

52:12.671 --> 52:14.256
Continued at the back.

52:15.507 --> 52:18.510
You may be a sore loser
who failed hard at love,

52:19.094 --> 52:22.430
but you succeeded in your career.
Let's work hard!

52:22.514 --> 52:26.226
It's me, Sol-i.

52:26.309 --> 52:28.478
Can you give me 20 million won please?

52:29.146 --> 52:30.689
- Jackass!
- Ow!

52:31.356 --> 52:33.024
Why did you kick me?

52:45.871 --> 52:47.164
Here you go.

52:47.247 --> 52:50.417
My dear, what have you
been doing these days?

52:50.500 --> 52:53.336
- I'm filming Ung and Yeon-su.
- The documentary?

52:53.420 --> 52:56.548
- Yes.
- Oh, my! Will it be on TV, then?

52:56.631 --> 52:58.508
Yes, of course.

52:58.592 --> 52:59.885
You boy.

53:16.193 --> 53:17.736
Why are you so early?

53:17.819 --> 53:19.321
Come. Let's take a ride.

53:20.071 --> 53:21.281
Are you half-asleep?

53:21.364 --> 53:23.408
You said you wanted
to feel some freedom, right?

53:24.034 --> 53:27.412
- Let's go get some fresh air.
- No, I wanna stay home.

53:29.372 --> 53:30.540
Hey!

53:31.374 --> 53:34.628
What are you doing? Are you trying
to wake the whole neighborhood?

53:34.711 --> 53:37.672
- Well, why shouldn't I?
- Cut if off! Don't do that!

53:37.756 --> 53:38.924
Just get in.

53:44.679 --> 53:46.473
In American horror films,

53:46.556 --> 53:50.143
crimes usually happen
suddenly in broad daylight.

53:54.147 --> 53:55.815
Going somewhere?

54:02.989 --> 54:04.199
Where are you going?

54:08.787 --> 54:10.038
What?

54:15.585 --> 54:20.215
When the victim is at his most vulnerable,
that's when they attack.

54:34.479 --> 54:36.273
And the criminal is usually…

54:37.816 --> 54:39.484
someone close to him.

54:46.074 --> 54:47.409
What are you doing?

55:22.027 --> 55:24.195
Choi Ung's guerilla gig!

55:24.279 --> 55:26.072
I wonder how many fans will be here today?

55:26.656 --> 55:29.409
All right. Get out. Get out!

55:29.492 --> 55:30.952
Come on, enjoy the view.

55:31.536 --> 55:33.246
What do you think you're doing?

55:33.330 --> 55:36.624
You didn't say a single word
during the whole four-hour drive!

55:36.708 --> 55:37.709
What…

55:38.418 --> 55:40.962
Hey! Where's your boss right now, huh?
I'm going to sue…

55:48.720 --> 55:51.014
- Hey, Kim Ji-ung!
- Move!

55:52.140 --> 55:53.433
You got here safe.

55:53.516 --> 55:56.811
Hey, Kim Ji-ung. This prank
is neither fun, nor impressive, okay.

55:56.895 --> 56:00.190
I have no idea
what you're trying to do here, but…

56:06.071 --> 56:09.574
So the genre of this
isn't really romance…

56:11.576 --> 56:14.829
Well, guess we're all here now.
We'll be staying here for three days.

56:16.039 --> 56:17.665
Wow, we have seven fans today!

56:17.749 --> 56:19.834
- …it's actually horror.
- Round of applause!

56:21.336 --> 56:24.172
I'm sure you've noticed,
but you can't leave without a car.

56:24.839 --> 56:27.300
If you wanna go home,
you'll have to walk all the way.

56:28.009 --> 56:29.344
It will take you days, though.

56:29.427 --> 56:30.887
Hey, Kim Ji-ung!

56:34.974 --> 56:37.102
A cliche horror-thriller film…

56:37.769 --> 56:39.104
that always releases…

56:39.813 --> 56:41.314
at this time of year.

56:47.737 --> 56:49.364
EPILOGUE

56:49.447 --> 56:50.573
- Hey, sir.
- Hmm.

56:50.657 --> 56:52.075
Choi Ung isn't here today.

56:53.535 --> 56:55.453
- What? He's not here?
- No.

56:57.580 --> 57:00.792
No wonder he wasn't picking up earlier.

57:10.051 --> 57:11.302
Uh, excuse me, sir.

57:12.220 --> 57:13.221
Yes?

57:14.139 --> 57:16.724
Will it be okay for me
to leave school early?

57:16.808 --> 57:18.268
Why? Are you feeling sick?

57:20.103 --> 57:21.020
Yes.

57:21.104 --> 57:23.898
Right. You must be overworked
with studying and filming lately.

57:23.982 --> 57:25.442
Sure. Go and get some rest.

57:32.073 --> 57:33.324
NO LONGER HUMAN
CHEKHOV SHORT STORIES

57:44.002 --> 57:44.836
Hi.

57:48.506 --> 57:50.008
Why are you here?

57:50.800 --> 57:51.718
Getting a book.

57:52.385 --> 57:54.179
You ran away from school and went here?

57:55.096 --> 57:56.347
No one would have guessed.

57:57.474 --> 57:58.808
What are you doing here?

58:00.643 --> 58:01.686
They let me off.

58:06.191 --> 58:07.817
Are you reading that book?

58:09.444 --> 58:10.278
Hmm.

58:11.946 --> 58:14.574
Okay, then it might be
a bit difficult for you.

58:14.657 --> 58:16.075
Are you sure you can read it?

58:16.159 --> 58:18.578
That is Nietzsche's
philosophical ideology.

58:18.661 --> 58:20.288
It won't be easy to understand.

58:21.623 --> 58:22.874
THUS SPOKE ZARATHUSTRA

58:24.459 --> 58:27.712
So are you giving me that?
It'll be better if I read it instead.

58:28.588 --> 58:29.881
Eternal recurrence.

58:29.964 --> 58:33.092
It's the concept that
the universe is recurring infinitely.

58:34.427 --> 58:37.138
In eternal recurrence,
all existence is recurring

58:37.222 --> 58:39.766
and will continue
to recur indefinitely forever.

58:39.849 --> 58:43.186
I got curious recently
about the eternity of time.

58:43.269 --> 58:44.479
So I'm reading it again.

58:49.692 --> 58:50.777
Okay.

58:51.444 --> 58:52.779
Return it when you're finished.

58:54.030 --> 58:55.281
About yesterday…

58:56.199 --> 58:57.575
I guess…

58:58.826 --> 59:01.287
I was a bit harsh to you.

59:05.583 --> 59:06.918
Is that why you ran away?

59:07.919 --> 59:09.921
Hmm. I thought you'd be uncomfortable.

59:16.219 --> 59:18.429
I'm hungry. Let's go eat together.

59:21.975 --> 59:28.982
CATCH ME IF YOU CAN

59:50.253 --> 59:52.380
Which trip
was the most memorable for you?

59:52.463 --> 59:54.841
I think I'm in love with you.

59:54.924 --> 59:57.635
We finally went on another one, huh?
And it's farther.

59:57.719 --> 59:59.637
- I'm very disappointed.
- NJ, hey!

59:59.721 --> 01:00:01.514
Gotta say, I'm a little confused.

01:00:01.598 --> 01:00:04.601
I'm wondering if you're showing
all these emotions because…

01:00:04.684 --> 01:00:06.185
We're not going to break up.

01:00:07.145 --> 01:00:08.938
Just come to me like you did today.
